    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nI would use Cloud migration when the problem matches the behavior it provides: Cloud migration moves applications, data, or infrastructure to cloud services while managing dependencies, security, cost, and cutover risk. A concrete application is Migrate a workload after understanding its dependencies, operational requirements, data movement, security controls, and rollback path.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis tests whether you can translate the concept into an engineering decision rather than reciting its definition.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Identify the requirement.\n2. Check that Cloud migration provides the required behavior: Cloud migration moves applications, data, or infrastructure to cloud services while managing dependencies, security, cost, and cutover risk.\n3. Apply it in a concrete case: Migrate a workload after understanding its dependencies, operational requirements, data movement, security controls, and rollback path.\n4. Reassess the choice if the workload or constraints change: For Cloud migration, the useful benefit has to be weighed against the extra complexity, maintenance, or cost introduced by the approach.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nStart with the requirement, then explain why Cloud migration fits it. I would give the concrete example and mention the main limitation so the answer shows judgment, not just tool familiarity.\n\n**Example :**\nMigrate a workload after understanding its dependencies, operational requirements, data movement, security controls, and rollback path.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA platform-scale architecture may use Cloud migration when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, migrate a workload after understanding its dependencies, operational requirements, data movement, security controls, and rollback path. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating Cloud migration as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with Cloud migration.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nDescribe the requirement that led you to choose it. “I would use it because it is popular” is much weaker than explaining the actual problem.",
